{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.onroad_activity",
    "description": "Template library: the shapes the ONROAD rates-first chain reuses, from docs/mixed-onroad.md §4. Five of them, and each is here rather than inline for a reason that document measures.\n\n`weeks_per_month` is WeeksInMonthHelper (crates/moves-calculators/src/generators/totalactivitygenerator/vmt.rs:115), a bare divisor. It is NOT lib/conversion.esm's `temporal_scale`, which is NONROAD's `mthf * 7 * dayf / ndays`; the two carry the same 7 and the same ndays and combine them differently, and merging them would double-apply a monthly factor. Omitting this divisor multiplies every onroad row by 4.43 for a 31-day month (§6.6).\n\n`share_of_group` is the normalisation of travel.rs:99-103 and :200-204, with the zero-denominator guard those lines carry. Three call sites. The guard is the difference between a group with no members and a NaN that propagates into every downstream product.\n\n`onroad_scc` is the third built identifier in this port, beside `pol_process_id` and `scc_zero_tail`. An onroad SCC is COMPUTED from four dimension columns (crates/moves-framework/src/execution/engine.rs:1450-1477), not looked up: the `scc` table's 14,976 rows agree with the formula and are read by nothing in the chain. Only the non-off-network branch is here; roadTypeID 100 is a different formula (source type + 1, literal \"00\" in the road slot) and would be a separate template.\n\n`source_bin_*_of` unpack a packed `sourceBinID`. The forward packing is deliberately absent: the id is 1e18 + fuel*1e16 + engTech*1e14 + regClass*1e12 + shortModYrGroup*1e10, about 1.01e18, which is past 2^53, so a document must key on the components and never materialise the id (docs/mixed-onroad.md §2.2, and finding F18 for the same hazard one exponent lower). The INVERSE is safe and is needed, because `emissionrate`'s 69,200 rows arrive with the id already packed and carry no component columns: `floor(bin/1e16)` has a small exact quotient even though `bin` itself is not exactly representable.\n\n`ev_energy_divisor` is adjust.rs:689-708. It is named because §2.3(f) measures it as the single largest correction in the fixture -- up to 22.1% on the electricity rows -- and because it is the one step `moves.rs` computes and then does not apply, so a port that followed the Rust rather than the snapshot would omit it silently.\n\nDeliberately NOT here: `clamp(x, 0, 1)`. It appears twice in the chain, at §2.3(d) and §2.3(e), with different bodies either side and different constants inside, and the VALUE each clamp takes is the load-bearing fact in both cases. A `clamp01` template would hide which clamp is which. As with every library here, an `enums` block does not cross a template import (esm-spec §9.3, finding F3), so identifier values arrive as parameters that the call site binds to `enum` ops.\n\n`is_energy_pollutant` and `energy_unit_divisor` are the two halves of engine.rs:1286-1310, the only place in the onroad chain where a unit conversion is conditional on WHICH pollutant a row carries: kilojoules become Million BTU for pollutants 91, 92 and 93 and for nothing else. They are here rather than inline because a fixture that emits one pollutant-process divides unconditionally and every fixture that emits several has to test, so the membership rule -- three ids, of which a typical run selects one -- would otherwise be rewritten once per multi-pollutant fixture and would have three chances to lose the two ids that are not in the run. The divisor arrives as a parameter rather than being applied inside `is_energy_pollutant` so that the predicate stays a predicate: `rspp_isEnergy` is asserted in its own right, and the caller binds `kilojoules_per_million_btu` to the second parameter.\n\n`link_travel_hours_share` is the one PROJECT-domain shape here: `ProjectTAG.allocateTotalActivityBasis`'s `least(linkLength / linkAvgSpeed, 1.0)` (ProjectTAG.java:354-368), the share of the hour a vehicle entering a link spends on it, capped at the hour. A link whose average speed is not positive gets 1 -- the SQL's `else` arm keeps the volume and drops the factor rather than dividing by zero. It is the only place the onroad chain turns a link's geometry into time (PLAN.md §7.3.40).\n\n`off_network_idle_sho` is TotalActivityGenerator step 190c, the SHO of the off-network road type: `S (tif - SD/S) / (1 - tif)`, floored at 0, with S the zone's on-network SHO, SD the same weighted by each road type's driving-idle fraction and tif `totalIdleFraction` -- the off-network idling that brings a vehicle's total idle share to tif, given what its network driving already holds. In the SQL's association (`TotalActivityGenerator.java`, the step-190 insert into `SHO`); `tif = 1` and an empty network (`sum(sho)` 0, a NULL in the SQL) give 0. A template because the ratio and its two guards are one fact, and a caller that wrote it inline would have three chances to drop a guard (PLAN.md §7.3.46).\n\n`kilojoules_per_million_btu` is MOVES' 1055.0559 J/BTU x 10^6 / 1000, a pure NUMBER, because most callers divide by it inside a `rspp_unitDivisor`-style selection whose other arm is 1 -- the divisor of an energy pollutant and of a mass pollutant in one variable, which cannot carry a unit (esm-spec §4.8.6). `million_btu_energy` is the same number times one kJ: the energy of one million BTU, for a caller whose numerator IS declared `kJ` (components/onroad_energy_output.esm's `out_emissionQuant`, runs/mixed_onroad_run.esm's `run_emissionQuant`), so that `kJ / million_btu_energy` is a checked count of million BTU. Multiplying by 1.0 changes no bit.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "activity", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "days_per_week": {
      "params": [],
      "body": 7.0
    },
    "weeks_per_month": {
      "params": ["days_in_month"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          "days_in_month",
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "days_per_week", "bindings": {} }
        ]
      }
    },
    "share_of_group": {
      "params": ["numerator", "group_total"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["group_total", 0.0] },
          { "op": "/", "args": ["numerator", "group_total"] },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "onroad_scc": {
      "params": ["fuel_type_id", "source_type_id", "road_type_id", "process_id"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [22.0, 100000000.0] },
          { "op": "+", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["fuel_type_id", 1000000.0] },
            { "op": "+", "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": ["source_type_id", 10000.0] },
              { "op": "+", "args": [
                { "op": "*", "args": ["road_type_id", 100.0] },
                "process_id"
              ] }
            ] }
          ] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "source_bin_slot": {
      "params": ["source_bin_id", "slot_scale"],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          { "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["source_bin_id", "slot_scale"] }] },
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            100.0,
            { "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": [
              { "op": "floor", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["source_bin_id", "slot_scale"] }] },
              100.0 ] }] }
          ] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "ev_energy_divisor": {
      "params": ["battery_efficiency", "charging_efficiency", "is_electric"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["is_electric", 0.0] },
          { "op": "max", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["battery_efficiency", "charging_efficiency"] },
            1.0e-300 ] },
          1.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "kilojoules_per_million_btu": {
      "params": [],
      "body": { "op": "/", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": [1055.0559, 1000000.0] }, 1000.0] }
    },
    "million_btu_energy": {
      "params": [],
      "body": { "op": "*", "args": [
        { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "kilojoules_per_million_btu", "bindings": {} },
        { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": 1.0, "units": "kJ" }] }
    },
    "is_energy_pollutant": {
      "params": ["pollutant_id", "total_energy_id", "petroleum_energy_id", "fossil_fuel_energy_id"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "or", "args": [
            { "op": "==", "args": ["pollutant_id", "total_energy_id"] },
            { "op": "or", "args": [
              { "op": "==", "args": ["pollutant_id", "petroleum_energy_id"] },
              { "op": "==", "args": ["pollutant_id", "fossil_fuel_energy_id"] } ] } ] },
          1.0,
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "energy_unit_divisor": {
      "params": ["is_energy", "energy_divisor"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["is_energy", 0.5] },
          "energy_divisor",
          1.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "link_travel_hours_share": {
      "params": ["link_length", "link_avg_speed"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["link_avg_speed", 0.0] },
          { "op": "min", "args": [{ "op": "/", "args": ["link_length", "link_avg_speed"] }, 1.0] },
          1.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "off_network_idle_sho": {
      "params": ["network_sho", "driving_idle_sho", "total_idle_fraction"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "and", "args": [
            { "op": "<", "args": ["total_idle_fraction", 1.0] },
            { "op": ">", "args": ["network_sho", 0.0] }
          ] },
          { "op": "max", "args": [
            { "op": "/", "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": [
                "network_sho",
                { "op": "-", "args": ["total_idle_fraction", { "op": "/", "args": ["driving_idle_sho", "network_sho"] }] }
              ] },
              { "op": "-", "args": [1.0, "total_idle_fraction"] }
            ] },
            0.0
          ] },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
